  <items>
    <headline level="1" number="4.2">Stem changing verbs:</headline>
    <headline level="2"> e -> ie, o -> ue</headline>
    <headline level="3">TBD</headline>
    <paragraph starting_point="ANTE TODO" sidebar_ref="1">
      Stem changing verbs deviate from the normal pattern of regular verbs. When stem changing verbs are conjugated, they have a vowel change in the last syllable of the stem
    </paragraph>
    <paragraph bullet="true">
      <attention /> In many verbs, such as <b>empezar</b> <i>(to begin)</i>, the stem vowel changes from <b>e</b> to <b>ie</b>.
      Note that the <b>nosotros/as</b> and <b>vosotros/as</b> forms don't have a stem change.
    </paragraph>
